**# NAT/PAT Configuration**
NAT overload was configured on R1 to allow internal private IP addresses to communicate with the simulated external network.
The internal interface was configured as:
```text
ip nat inside
```
The WAN interface was configured as:
```text
ip nat outside
```
NAT overload was configured using the WAN interface address.
This allows multiple internal devices to share the router's external IP address when accessing the simulated external network.

